{
  "info": {
    "name": "Sri Raghavendra Swamy Matha API",
    "description": "API collection for Sri Raghavendra Swamy Matha temple management system. Includes events, AI chat, knowledge base, donations, bookings, and admin APIs.\n\n## Authentication\n\n### Admin APIs\nAdmin APIs require Firebase ID token authentication. To get a token:\n\n1. **Option A - Via Browser (Recommended)**\n   - Log into the admin portal at https://sri-raghavendra-mutt.vercel.app/admin\n   - Open DevTools (F12) → Application → Local Storage\n   - Copy the `firebase:authUser` token or the `idToken`\n\n2. **Option B - Via Firebase Auth REST API**\n   ```bash\n   curl -X POST 'https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signInWithPassword?key=YOUR_API_KEY' \\\n     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n     -d '{\"email\":\"admin@example.com\",\"password\":\"password\",\"returnSecureToken\":true}'\n   ```\n\n3. **Option C - Via Seed API Key (Limited routes)**\n   Some routes accept `x-admin-api-key` header with the `ADMIN_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n### Using the Token in Postman\n\nFor admin requests, add the following header:\n```\nAuthorization: Bearer YOUR_FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN\n```\n\nSet the token as a variable `{{firebaseToken}}` in Postman.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://sri-raghavendra-mutt.vercel.app",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "localUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "firebaseToken",
